# Components and pages

## Page anatomy

Every list page follows the same pattern (see `features/organization/branches-page.tsx`):

```tsx
<PageHeader title={t('x.title')} description={t('x.subtitle')} actions={<Can permission="x:create">…</Can>} />
<DataTable columns={columns} data={data?.data} meta={data?.meta} isLoading={isLoading} state={table} onExport={…} />
<SimpleFormDialog … />   // or a dedicated form dialog for complex forms
```

- `useTableState()` holds page/size/sort/search and produces the query params; pass `{ query: tableQuery }` to keep the previous page visible while loading.
- Columns are memoised with `useMemo<ColumnDef<Dto, unknown>[]>` and depend on `t`.
- Exports use `exportTable(format, fileName, columns, rows)` behind an `ExportMenu` (Excel / PDF; DataTable's
  `onExport(format)` renders it) with `fetchAllPages` so all filtered rows are exported, not just the visible page.
  pdfmake is imported lazily in `export-pdf.ts`; never import it statically.
- Destructive actions use `ConfirmDialog`; status values use `ToneBadge` / `ActiveBadge` / domain badges (`WorkflowStatusBadge`).
- Detail pages: back link, `PageHeader` with a status badge, two-column grid (`lg:grid-cols-3`) of `Card`s.
- Detail fields use `InfoCard` / `Field` from `shared/components/info-card.tsx`.
- Money: API decimals are strings; render them with `formatMoney(value, currency)`, never `Number(...).toFixed`.
  Quantities use `formatQuantity(value, unitCode)`.
- Choosing a stock item (product variant) always goes through `ItemPicker` from
  `features/inventory/inventory-components.tsx` (server-side search, optional `warehouseId` / `inStock`).
- Choosing a business partner goes through `PartnerPicker` / `PartnerField` from `features/partners/partner-components.tsx`.
- Trade documents (quotes, orders, invoices) share `features/trade/`: `DocumentLinesEditor` (editable priced lines,
  `fixedItems` / `maxQuantity` when lines come from a source document), `DocumentLinesTable` (read-only lines with
  extra columns), `DocumentTotals`, `document-math.ts` (client totals mirror the API) and `DocumentLink`.
  Document permissions may be any-of: `Can`, `usePermission` and `requirePermission` accept a code array.
- Barcode / QR scanning: a text input with `autoFocus` (USB scanners type and press Enter) plus, when
  `cameraScanSupported()`, the `CameraScanner` dialog from `shared/components/camera-scanner.tsx` (native `BarcodeDetector`).
- Matrix screens (timesheet, shift roster) are plain `<table>`s inside a horizontally scrolling `Card` with a
  `sticky left-0 bg-card` first column; compact day cells carry details in `title` / `aria-label`.
- Printable documents (e.g. `features/assets/assignment-document-page.tsx`) are normal routes: toolbars get `print:hidden`,
  the paper uses `print:` overrides; the app shell hides itself in print media. "PDF" is the browser's print-to-PDF.

## shadcn/ui

- Add primitives with `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <name>`; they land in `src/shared/ui`. After adding, make sure imports use `@/shared/lib/utils` for `cn`.
- Do not fork primitives for one screen; compose them in `shared/components` or the feature folder.

## Styling

- Tailwind utility classes only; merge conditional classes with `cn()`.
- Use theme tokens (`bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-primary`) so light/dark mode keeps working; avoid raw hex colours.
- Icons from `lucide-react`; buttons with an icon put the icon first (`<Plus /> {label}`).
- Responsive by default: grids collapse to one column on mobile, tables scroll horizontally.

## Accessibility

- Icon-only buttons need `aria-label`.
- Form controls are always wrapped in `FormItem` + `FormLabel` so labels are associated (E2E tests rely on `getByLabel`).
